    "background_story": "Elena was a renowned zoologist with a passion for studying lagomorphs, a group of mammals that includes rabbits and hares. Growing up in the countryside, she was fascinated by the gentle creatures that hopped through her family's garden. Her love for lagomorphs led her to dedicate her career to understanding their behavior, habitat, and social structures. Elena's groundbreaking research on the European rabbit helped conservation efforts and earned her international recognition. She became known as the 'Lagomorph Lady' among her peers, and her work inspired a new generation of scientists to explore the fascinating world of these often-overlooked creatures. Elena's dedication to her field was a testament to the power of following one's passion and making a meaningful impact on the world.",
